From 280b82099c5d76a582e29171c90b218b630393d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Junction 2026 team <junction2026@localhost>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:26:02 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] feat(ui): capture a state snapshot with a hotkey in live
 sessions

A new hotkey action, "Capture state snapshot" (Live session; Space by
default, rebindable in the settings), saves a snapshot of the live session
wherever one has an environment: the environment view, recording and
inference. The session provider mounts it for its own session, so the
snapshot is of what that page shows. A toast says where it was saved and
what it holds (cameras with color/depth, follower/leader joints, what could
not be captured), or why nothing was saved.

Space is left to a focused button, switch, checkbox or similar control that
Space activates, as typing in text fields already was; other hotkeys are
unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
